several exist is not specified, but the same input always"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives the same cut. When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the cut"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(all of capacity zero). Parallel capacities add; self-loops are ignored. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work (self-loops are never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asked). O(nm log n) in the worst case, far less when contractions are many."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Flows3CutV","text":"Cut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedViewV","text":"DirectedView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">?"}]},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/Graph/edmondsKarpMaximumFlow(from:to:capacity:)":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximum flow over "},{"code":"directed","type